module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.LinearlyReductiveGroupScheme
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Cartesian.Mod
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Smooth
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.FiniteType
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.ClosedImmersion
public import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IsAlgClosed.Basic
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.DenseRestrictionSemisimple
import WeilConjectures.AlgebraicGeometry.Regular
import WeilConjectures.Mathlib.RingTheory.Nullstellensatz

/-! # Smooth common fixed schemes of dense subgroups

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Lemma 13.6 and Theorem 13.7, printed p.256
(blueprint: lem-sfb-linearly-reductive-dense-fixed-smooth).

The fixed functor is tested on every commutative algebra, including nonreduced ones.
Linear reductivity uses the existing scheme-theoretic invariant-subspace definition.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory
open scoped MonObj

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A closed scheme representing the common fixed functor of a dense abstract subgroup
of a smooth affine linearly reductive group acting on a smooth affine scheme is smooth.
Neither scheme is required to be connected.

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), Lemma 13.6 and Theorem 13.7, printed p.256
(blueprint: lem-sfb-linearly-reductive-dense-fixed-smooth).

Proof:
1. Write X = Spec B and F = Spec (B/I), using def-weil-closed-immersion. The quotient
   is finite type. By lem-wf-affine-nullstellensatz-vanishing, every closed point x of F
   is k-rational. The local ring A = O_{X,x} is regular by
   lem-weil-pbc-smooth-scheme-over-field-regular. Write m for its maximal ideal.
2. Apply lem-sfb-dense-fixed-local-ideal-jets. It identifies O_{F,x} with A/J, where
   J is generated by gamma*f-f for gamma in Gamma and f in m, and supplies the rational
   finite jets R_n = A/m^(n+1), M_n = m/m^(n+1), V = m/m^2 and the equivariant
   surjection q_n : M_n -> V. Inverse pullbacks give the same ideal.
3. Linear reductivity decomposes each jet into simple rational summands.
   By lem-sfb-dense-restriction-semisimple these stay semisimple on Gamma and q_n has
   an equivariant section. Decompose V into its trivial part V_0 and nontrivial simple
   summands V_i. Their lifted images W_i in M_n have the same properties.
4. For i > 0 the span of gamma*w-w in W_i is invariant and nonzero, hence all of W_i.
   Thus W_i lies in J_n, the image of J in R_n. Choose bases with the nontrivial
   vectors first (s vectors), then lift them to u_1,...,u_d in m. Their cotangent
   classes form a basis of V.
5. Successive substitution modulo m^a expresses every element of R_n as a polynomial
   in these lifted vectors plus a scalar. The ideal L_n of the first s vectors lies
   in J_n. Modulo L_n the remaining generators are fixed, so every difference vanishes.
   Hence J_n = L_n, or J+m^(n+1) = (u_1,...,u_s)+m^(n+1).
6. The integer s is independent of n. Apply lem-sfb-regular-quotient-parameter-approximation
   to deduce regularity of A/J. The tuples may depend on n. This includes s=0, s=d, d=0.
7. By lem-sfb-regular-separable-affine-smooth-neighbourhood, every closed point of F
   has a smooth open neighbourhood: its residue field is k, hence separable over k.
   Their union has closed complement containing no closed point, hence empty by
   lem-sc-lft-over-field-jacobson-space. The neighbourhoods cover F, so
   lem-weil-pbc-smooth-local-on-source gives smoothness. Its empty-cover case covers
   empty F. No connectedness or irreducibility was used. -/
theorem linearlyReductive_dense_fixed_smooth
    {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    (G : Over (Spec (.of k))) [GrpObj G] [IsAffine G.left]
    [Smooth G.hom] [LocallyOfFiniteType G.hom] [QuasiCompact G.hom]
    (hG : IsLinearlyReductiveGroupScheme G)
    (Γ : Subgroup (points G k))
    (hdense : DenseRange fun g : Γ ↦ g.val.left (IsLocalRing.closedPoint k))
    (X : Over (Spec (.of k))) [IsAffine X.left]
    [Smooth X.hom] [LocallyOfFiniteType X.hom] [QuasiCompact X.hom]
    [action : ModObj G X]
    (F : Over (Spec (.of k))) (i : F ⟶ X) [IsClosedImmersion i.left]
    (hfixed : ∀ (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra k A] (x : points X A),
      (∃ z : points F A, z ≫ i = x) ↔
        ∀ g : Γ, points.map G (Algebra.ofId k A) g.val • x = x) :
    Smooth F.hom := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
